  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1201 AM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nThursday into Friday, an upper level ridge centered over \nsoutheastern Texas will be the dominant driver of our weather, \nkeeping us mainly dry and continued warmer than normal, with highs\nmainly in the 90s, lows in the upper 60s/lower 70s, and generally\ndry weather. Although we will be mainly dry, there will be a low \nchance (20%) for showers and thunderstorms along our western CWA \nborder. Although an upper level trough will move through the \nplains Friday into Saturday, slightly weakening the ridge, we will\nremain hot, with highs in the mid to upper 90s Saturday into \nMonday, and mainly dry conditions. \n\nThe past couple medium range model runs have shown a stronger \ntrough moving through the central and southern plains Tuesday, \npotentially bringing the first significant cold front into the \narea Tuesday night into Wednesday, along with a chance of \nprecipitation.",
